/T (After the initial pilot, the methodology was extended to incorporate climate projections data. Using an initial sample of five crops \(barley, poppies, potatoes and wine grapes\) \(sparkling and table wine\), current climate data in the model was replaced by climate projection data from the Climate Futures for Tasmania dataset. These layers demonstrate the suitability of crops under future climate scenarios. This was later extended to cover the remaining 27 ESM crops.    )
/E (After the initial pilot, the methodology was extended to incorporate climate projections data. Using an initial sample of five crops \(barley, poppies, potatoes and wine grapes\) \(sparkling and table wine\), current climate data in the model was replaced by climate projection data from the Climate Futures for Tasmania dataset. These layers demonstrate the suitability of crops under future climate scenarios. This was later extended to cover the remaining 27 ESM crops.    )
