504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Thanks to the extensive data that sits behind the maps, the ESM are believed by interviewees to be accurate in predicting these climate risks.  )
/Alt ()
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( )
/Alt ()
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Evidence from this case study also suggests growers use the ESM products themselves to inform decision making. Here it is important to understand landowners and growers can range from small hold landowners to large scale enterprises with multiple properties of interest. Both types of growers have made use of the maps to gain a high-level understanding of their land, although their ability to drill down further depends on experience with GIS and technical capacity. Brown Family Wine Group have used the ESM in their climate adaptation journey outlined above \(example 1\) including to compare locations, help choose suitable grape varieties and identify new land for investment. The example from Dalness Estate \(example 2\) also demonstrates a case where the ESM were used to direct new development.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
