515 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Example 2: Using the ESM for new vineyard development at Dalness Estate)
/E (Example 2: Using the ESM for new vineyard development at Dalness Estate)
/Alt ()
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
516 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Dalness Estate is a large historic property over 1700 hectares. In 2017, the estate contracted a consultant to identify a suitable location for a new vineyard on the property. The ESM maps were used to narrow down areas on the property that could be suitable and analyse potential risk factors.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
517 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Two suitable locations were identified: one was cheaper to develop but slightly higher risk for wine growing, and the other was more expensive to develop due to its location and terrain. The owner chose to develop the more affordable site, but after initial success proceeded to develop the second site.   )
/Alt ()
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Several years later, both vineyards are performing well and have not suffered from frost \(though it is likely the higher-risk site will on occasion\). In total, they now have developed close to 40 hectares of vineyard and investment is estimated to be greater than $4 million. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
519 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This is a clear example of a project which has used maps in decision making and future planning for a vineyard, which also led to a positive impact on the surrounding district, including an increase in local employment. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
