528 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The project team analysed interviews and documents to better understand some of the factors enabling both the ESM project and the adaptation taken by wine growers. Understanding some of the significant barriers that were overcome provides important context to these enabling factors. While enabling factors are not necessarily the inverse of barriers, evidence suggests they do assist in circumnavigating barriers. )
/Alt ()
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
529 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The most significant barrier faced by the developers of the new methodology for DSM and ESM was scepticism about the accuracy and usefulness of the product. The agricultural industry was loyal to traditional soil sampling and mapping, a very resource intensive, expensive and subjective exercise that is difficult to execute state-wide. This is discussed by Kidd et al. \(8\). Alongside the scepticism, additional work was required to get industry onboard with committing the significant investment of time and resources that was needed for quality engagement.   )
/Alt ()
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
